      "candidate": "```python\n# Repaired scraper for https://example.test/gpu-1\n# This script uses a pure\u2011Python static selector approach and returns\n# a plain Python dict that satisfies the `gpu-price-schema-v1` schema.\n# 1. The price is now parsed as a float (previously int) \u2013 the schema\n#    expects a numeric type that can be fractional.  \n# 2. All extracted values are stripped of whitespace and unnecessary\n#    characters before conversion.  \n# 3. The scraper no longer returns a `mappingproxy`; it returns a normal\n#    dict, which prevents the \u201ccontrolled mutation M001\u201d failure caused by\n#    the previous proxy wrapper.\n\nimport requests\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n\nURL = \"https://example.test/gpu-1\"\n\ndef _parse_price(text: str) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Convert `$599` or `599` to 599.0\"\"\"\n    return float(text.replace(\"$\", \"\").replace(\",\", \"\").strip())\n\ndef _normalize_availability(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the canonical availability value.\"\"\"\n    txt = text.lower().strip()\n    if \"in stock\" in txt:\n        return \"in_stock\"\n    return \"out_of_stock\"\n\ndef scrape() -> dict:\n    response = requests.get(URL, timeout=10)\n    response.raise_for_status()\n\n    soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, \"html.parser\")\n\n    product_id = soup.select_one('meta[itemprop=\"sku\"]')['content'].strip()\n    title = soup.select_one('h1.product-title').get_text(strip=True)\n    price = _parse_price(soup.select_one('.price').get_text())\n    availability = _normalize_availability(soup.select_one('.availability').get_text())\n    rating = float(soup.select_one('.rating').get_text().strip())\n    url = soup.select_one('link[rel=\"canonical\"]')['href'].strip()\n\n    # Build the final result in the exact order expected by the schema\n    return {\n        \"product_id\": product_id,\n        \"title\": title,\n        \"price\": price,\n        \"availability\": availability,\n        \"rating\": rating,\n        \"url\": url,\n    }\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    data = scrape()\n    print(data)\n```\n\n**Explanation of changes**\n\n* Converted `price` to a float value to match the schema\u2019s numeric expectation.\n* Normalized the availability text into the canonical `\"in_stock\"` or `\"out_of_stock\"` values.\n* Returned a plain dictionary instead of a `mappingproxy`, eliminating the mutation error."
    },
